#, fuzzy
msgctxt "lblPropertyDescription-refresh.evaluateContentChangesForModifiedFileMode:"
msgid "By default, SmartGit will check for file content changes even if the filemode has changed. If there are lots of filemode-only modifications of large files \\(e.g., LFS files\\), this may significantly worsen performance compared to command line Git status. In this case, you may set this property to `false`. Note that this will disable the distinction of 'Content' vs. 'File Mode' in the GUI."
